00:03:20.720 --> 00:03:22.950
<v Ira Glass>And we try to figure out the truth of them.

00:03:22.950 --> 00:03:25.410
<v Fred Armisen>(IMITATING IRA GLASS) And we try to figure out the truth of them.

00:03:25.410 --> 00:03:27.190
<v Ira Glass>One concerns two men who've never met--

00:03:27.190 --> 00:03:31.050
<v Fred Armisen>(IMITATING IRA GLASS) The other, two animals who never meet.

00:03:31.050 --> 00:03:40.000
<v Ira Glass>I think you should do the next part because it's so-- do you want to hear me do it first? Or do you just want to do it? From WBEZ Chicago, it's This American Life, distributed by Public Radio International.

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:42.480
<v Fred Armisen>(IMITATING IRA GLASS) Distributed by Public Radio International.

00:03:42.480 --> 00:03:44.450
<v Fred Armisen>[LAUGHTER]

00:03:44.450 --> 00:03:54.410
<v Ira Glass>I feel like a Muppet. Why does it make me feel like a Muppet, Fred? [LAUGHTER] Seriously, why--

00:03:54.410 --> 00:03:58.380
<v Fred Armisen>I think you could be a Muppet. I don't know why they don't have a Muppet of you.

00:03:58.380 --> 00:04:01.380
<v Ira Glass>From WBEZ Chicago, It's This American Life--

00:04:01.380 --> 00:04:04.120
